WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:03.210
Rhiannon: We all need to become
better at understanding, how we

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:07.290
can help children and young people
to thrive and be mentally healthy.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:11.070
By having resilience, children and
young people can gain the strength

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:15.589
to cope when something goes wrong and
have the ability to solve problems,

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:19.259
so they can remain mentally healthy,
or bounce back from times of stress.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:24.919
Leah: Family and social relationships,
self-esteem and personal values, aid

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.170
resilience and there are skills that
can be learnt to cope better with

00:00:28.179 --> 00:00:30.259
stress and improve resilience further.

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:34.330
Resilience in children and young
people can be boosted by support from

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:38.830
family, friends, neighbours and even
pets, as positive interactions with

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.660
those who are close can help relieve
stress and shape good memories.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.799
Rhiannon: Recalling good memories also
improves resilience in vulnerable young

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.630
people which helps them to better cope
with the stresses they’re experiencing,

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:54.050
such as remembering the fun times they
have had with their friends and family.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:59.300
Leah: Building resilience in young people
may help to protect against engaging in

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.310
health risk behaviour, such as smoking,
drinking alcohol, illicit drug use and

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:09.670
unprotected sex and can also help to delay
‘transitions’ such as parenthood, which

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:13.819
can in turn help to avoid the potential
negative health consequences of early

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:16.010
pregnancy for both parents and babies.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:20.380
Rhiannon: Resilience can contribute to
healthy behaviours, higher qualifications

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:24.899
and skills, better employment, better
mental wellbeing, and quicker or more

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.570
successful recovery from illness.

